  "description": "RUMTUS crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C108 H124 Dy11 N36 O42 5+,29.25(C1 H4 O1),0.1(H2 O1),5(N1 O3 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy7 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.574-5.316 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.37-170.18°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy11(HL2)8(μ3-OH)8(μ4-O)2(CH3O)4(NO3)4](NO3)5·18CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 5 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
